From: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 20:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] lib: hashtable: add per-iteration settle delay on sun5i/R8

On Allwinner sun5i/R8 (C.H.I.P.), U-Boot hangs inside the
himport_r() parse loop after NAND BBT scanning.  A one-time barrier
or delay before entering the loop is insufficient; the issue
requires settling time between iterations.

Debug UART puts() calls distributed through the loop body (each
~1.5 ms at 115200 baud) eliminated the hang, confirming per-
iteration timing is required.  The UART accesses target the APB0
bus which is separate from the AHB bus used by NAND and DRAM.

Add a 5 ms udelay per iteration when building for sun5i.  This is
compiled away to nothing on all other SoCs via IS_ENABLED().  Total
overhead for a ~30-variable environment is ~150 ms at boot, which
is acceptable.

Signed-off-by: SkiffOS <skiffos@skiffos.com>
---
 lib/hashtable.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/hashtable.c b/lib/hashtable.c
--- a/lib/hashtable.c
+++ b/lib/hashtable.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@
 #else				/* U-Boot build */
 # include <linux/string.h>
 # include <linux/ctype.h>
+# include <linux/delay.h>
 #endif

 #define USED_FREE 0
@@ -882,6 +883,14 @@
 	do {
 		struct env_entry e, *rv;

+		/*
+		 * Workaround for sun5i/R8 (C.H.I.P.): after NAND BBT scan the
+		 * AHB/MBUS bus needs settling time between env parse iterations.
+		 * A 5 ms gap matches the timing that debug UART puts() provided.
+		 */
+		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN5I))
+			udelay(5000);
+
 		/* skip leading white space */
 		while (isblank(*dp))
 			++dp;
